{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-sol","packSha":"f5f771967a3549b8a6fc168a157d74235b696939cfc4d6efd44aeee7239863af","packTokens":5608,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":5501,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":39,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement every HTTP operation declared in `contracts/openapi.yaml` at its declared path and method, with the declared request and response schemas, status codes, media types, and operation behavior.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A running API backed by a test database. when A client requests GET /openapi/v1.json. then The response document lists every contract path, method, operationId, schema, response status, and security declaration.\",\n    \"Given An isolated PostgreSQL App database contains contract-required fixtures and the test client has credentials for each contract-declared role. when A black-box contract suite calls every path-and-method pair in `contracts/openapi.yaml` with valid requests and declared validation, authentication, and authorization cases. then Each response status, media type, and body field value matches the corresponding contract operation, including its declared error responses.\",\n    \"Given A valid administrator-managed account, an authenticated client, and operational records exist. when The client signs in and requests GET /api/v1/overview, GET /api/v1/lots, GET /api/v1/lots/{lotId}/lifecycle, GET /api/v1/lots/{lotId}/performance, and GET /api/v1/lots/{lotId}/financials for existing lots. then The sign-in and operational response statuses are 200; the sign-in response contains user, accessToken, and availablePages; the overview response contains headline, activeLots, activePens, lots, inventory, rationFeeding, estimatedEnergyMcal, recentActivity, and recentSync; the list and lot responses contain their contract-defined procurement traceability, pen allocation, lifecycle milestones, weight history, projected market date, performance metrics, event history, cost breakdown, and recommendation fields.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client requests the lifecycle of a lot that does not exist. when The client calls GET /api/v1/lots/{lotId}/lifecycle with an unknown lot ID. then The response status is 404 and the response contains the contract's error and code fields.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement the inventory and ration operations declared in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, normalizing quantities and unit costs to pounds-based values while retaining entered units for display and treating one ton as 2,000 pounds.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated client and inventory records with stock movements exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/inventory and GET /api/v1/inventory/projections. then Each response status is 200; the inventory response list includes entered units, normalizedPounds, normalizedCostUsdPerLb, stock totals, and movements; and the projections response contains wastageRatio, remaining stock, daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month and annual projection fields, and movements.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client submits the contract example receipt of 2 tons at USD 360 per ton. when The client calls POST /api/v1/inventory/receipts. then The response status is 201 and the response fields retain enteredQuantity 2 and enteredUnit ton while reporting normalizedPounds 4000 and normalizedCostUsdPerLb 0.18.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client and saved rations exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/rations. then The response status is 200 and the response list includes ration names, intended animal ranges, nutrition and cost values, ingredient entered units, normalized quantities, proportions, and ingredient pricing fields.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client submits a valid ration with ingredients expressed in tons. when The client calls POST /api/v1/rations. then The response status is 201 and the returned ration retains each enteredUnit and includes normalized ingredient quantities, ingredient costs, dryMatterPercent, energyMcalPerLb, and costUsdPerLb.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client submits valid nutrition or animal-range constraints. when The client calls POST /api/v1/rations/optimization. then The response status is 200 and the response candidates contain ingredient proportions, cost, nutrition values, tradeoff, and Candidate status.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client explicitly accepts an existing optimization candidate. when The client calls POST /api/v1/rations/candidates/{candidateId}/save and POST /api/v1/rations/candidates/{candidateId}/assign. then Each response status is 200 and each response contains the requested candidateId and its Saved or Assigned status.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client submits an invalid receipt. when The client calls POST /api/v1/inventory/receipts. then The response status is 422 and the response contains the contract's error, code, and field validation information.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement the feeding-plan and feeding-activity operations declared in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, calculating feeding quantities, variances, ingredient consumption, costs, energy, and inventory deductions in pounds.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated client and dated plans for a pen containing animals from two lots exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/feeding-plans and submits a valid plan to POST /api/v1/feeding-plans. then The GET response status is 200 and its list includes delivery date, pen, ration, planned quantity, status, and lotAllocations; the POST response status is 201 and its returned plan contains planned quantity and a separate allocation for each lot whose quantities sum to the planned quantity.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client and saved feeding activities exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/feeding-activities. then The response status is 200 and the response list includes plannedQuantityLb, actualQuantityLb, varianceLb, inventoryConsumption, feedCostUsd, energyMcal, and lotAllocations.\",\n    \"Given A valid feeding request has a planned quantity of 900 lb, actual delivery of 950 lb, and serves two lots. when The client calls POST /api/v1/feeding-activities. then The response status is 201, the returned varianceLb is 50, and the response lotAllocations show a separate lot-specific delivered share for each lot with quantities summing to 950 lb.\",\n    \"Given A saved feeding activity exists. when The client updates it with PATCH /api/v1/feeding-activities/{activityId} and then cancels it with DELETE /api/v1/feeding-activities/{activityId}. then The update response status is 200 with recalculated variance and totals, the cancel response is 200 with status Canceled, and the inventoryTotals closingLb reflects the reversal.\",\n    \"Given A feeding activity would consume more inventory than is available and its closing stock and activity list are recorded before the request. when The client posts the feeding activity through /api/v1/feeding-activities. then The response status is 409 with the contract-defined insufficient-stock error, and the inventory row and feeding-activity list remain unchanged.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement the weight-measurement, yard-summary, feed-to-gain report, and report-export operations declared in `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated client and weight records exist for the selected scope. when The client requests GET /api/v1/weight-measurements with and without a lotId query parameter. then Each response status is 200 and each response contains measurement records and a date/averageWeightLb trend list.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client submits a valid measurement for an existing lot, or corrects a saved measurement. when The client calls POST /api/v1/weight-measurements or PATCH /api/v1/weight-measurements/{measurementId}. then The create response status is 201 and the correction response status is 200; each response contains the accepted or corrected measurement, updated or recalculated metrics, and trend fields.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client and active lot and pen records exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/yard-summary. then The response status is 200 and the response contains yard totals, active lot and pen counts, pen summaries, and lot summaries.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client and matching and nonmatching lot performance records exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/reports/feed-to-gain with supported date, breed, sex, or penId filters. then The response status is 200 and the rows list contains only matching lots while the filters field contains the known filter choices.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client and feed-to-gain report data exist. when The client requests GET /api/v1/reports/feed-to-gain/export with format=csv and format=pdf and report filters. then Each response status is 200; the CSV response file has text/csv content and the PDF response file has application/pdf content; and each file contains the matching report data.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement the administrator account, synchronization, and demo operations declared in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, with the contract-defined request and response fields, status codes, and authorization rules.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated client with the role permitted by the contract and existing accounts. when The client requests GET /api/v1/admin/accounts. then The response status is 200 and the accounts list contains the documented account fields.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client with the role permitted by the contract submits a valid new account or changes an existing account role or password. when The client calls POST /api/v1/admin/accounts or PATCH /api/v1/admin/accounts/{accountId}. then The create response status is 201 and the update response status is 200; each returned account and message field matches the contract and the updated account reflects the requested change.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client calls synchronization and the configured mock procurement source returns record outcomes. when The client calls POST /api/v1/admin/sync. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the source, Completed or Partial status, and record-level results with targetLots and error fields.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client requests demo materials or submits start=true. when The client calls GET /api/v1/admin/demo and POST /api/v1/admin/demo/flow. then Each response status is 200; the demo response contains operationalData, rules, and sections; and the flow response contains started, currentStep, stepTitle, and status fields.\",\n    \"Given A client without the role required by the contract calls an operation that declares administrator authorization. when The client requests that operation. then The response status is 403 and the response contains the contract's Forbidden error and code fields.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The API shall require bearer authentication for operations declaring it in the contract, leave sign-in unauthenticated, and enforce role authorization only where the contract declares role access.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid sign-in request and a protected contract operation are available. when The client calls sign-in without a bearer token, then calls the protected operation without a token, and calls it with a role that is not authorized where the contract declares role restrictions. then The sign-in response status is 200 for valid credentials, the protected response status is 401 without authentication, and the response status is 403 for a disallowed role where declared.\",\n    \"Given A client has no bearer token. when The client calls GET /api/v1/overview. then The response status is 401 and the response contains the contract's error and code fields.\",\n    \"Given A valid Operator bearer token and a valid Administrator bearer token are available. when Each client requests GET /api/v1/admin/accounts. then The Operator response status is 403 and its response error code is FORBIDDEN; the Administrator response status is 200 and its response contains an accounts list.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall persist contract-backed operational records in PostgreSQL through the configured `ConnectionStrings:App` connection and apply the required data model without deleting, resetting, or changing pre-existing records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The configured PostgreSQL App database contains a pre-existing row and is isolated from other test databases. when The API starts, applies its data model, and a client retrieves the corresponding record through its contract operation. then The original database row and its field values remain present and unchanged.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated client creates or updates a contract record. when The client repeats the corresponding list or detail API call after the operation and after an API restart using the same App connection string. then The response contains the persisted record and its stored field values, and the database row persists across the restart.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall execute `SeedData.Run` only when `Seed:Demo` is true and, on that run, populate every contract-backed data table with at least two believable rows derived from contract examples.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh App database has `Seed:Demo` set to true. when The API starts and its contract list operations are called. then A database row count of at least two exists in every contract-backed data table, and each contract list response contains at least one record.\",\n    \"Given A fresh App database has `Seed:Demo` set to false or is unset. when The API starts and a client calls contract list operations. then The response lists reflect only records created independently of demo seeding and no demo row is required by the test.\",\n    \"Given Demo seeding is enabled and has already been run once. when The demo-seeding run is repeated. then The database row count may include duplicate sample rows because seed idempotency is not required.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is true, the Feedlot API shall insert two or three believable sample rows derived from contract examples into every contract domain table; repeated runs may insert duplicate sample rows.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL App database is configured with Seed:Demo true. when The API starts and contract list operations are queried. then Database row counts show two or three sample rows in every contract domain table, the seeded field values correspond to contract examples, and each supported list response contains sample data.\",\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL App database is configured with Seed:Demo false or the setting is unset. when The API starts and a client calls contract list operations. then The database contains no demo rows and the response lists reflect only records created independently of demo seeding.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the test factory starts an application without an explicit demo-seed opt-in, the test factory shall configure `Seed:Demo` as false.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh test-factory database and no explicit demo-seed opt-in. when The factory starts the API and a client requests a contract list. then The response contains no demo-seed rows and the database contains no rows inserted by SeedData.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When inventory, ration, or feeding calculations use quantities expressed in different units, the API shall convert quantities to pounds using 2,000 pounds per ton and retain entered units in returned display values.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The inventory contains Ground corn and a receipt is entered as 2 tons. when The client records the receipt and retrieves inventory. then The receipt response contains normalizedPounds of 4000 and retains enteredUnit as ton; the inventory response shows 2 in entered quantity, ton in enteredUnit, and 4000 in normalizedPounds and closingLb.\",\n    \"Given A ration ingredient or feeding quantity is entered in tons. when The API calculates ration costs, feed consumption, and inventory deductions. then The response shows quantities and deductions calculated using 2,000 pounds per ton while retaining the entered unit in returned display fields.\",\n    \"Given Inventory has a known closing stock in pounds and a ration whose ingredients include quantities entered in tons. when The client records a feeding activity using that ration and retrieves inventory and activity responses. then The inventory row reflects deductions calculated in pounds, and returned values for entered quantities retain their entered units.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a pen-level delivery serves animals from multiple lots, the API shall represent each lot's share as a distinct, separately attributable lot allocation containing only that lot's share.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A pen has allocations for two lots and a 950-pound feeding activity allocates 570 pounds to one lot and 380 pounds to the other. when The client records the activity and retrieves the activity response. then The activity response contains one allocation per lot with delivered quantities of 570 and 380 pounds and lot totals attributed only to their respective shares.\",\n    \"Given A valid feeding request has a planned quantity of 900 lb, actual delivery of 950 lb, and serves two lots. when The client calls POST /api/v1/feeding-activities. then The response lotAllocations show a separate lot-specific delivered share for each lot with quantities summing to 950 lb.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a pen-level delivery serves animals from multiple lots, the API shall record a separate feeding activity per lot containing only that lot's share of the delivered feed.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A pen contains two lots and a valid delivery request allocates 600 lb to one lot and 400 lb to the other. when The delivery is posted to POST /api/v1/feeding-activities and the feeding activities are then listed. then The response contains a separate activity record for each lot, each record contains only its lot's allocated quantity, and the returned activity quantities total 1000 lb.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot Operations API shall provide the contract functionality through HTTP operations without implementing separate feedlot product screens in this repository.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is running in this repository. when A person visits its available web routes. then The screen shows API documentation or health information only and no feedlot product screen is displayed.\",\n    \"Given The API is running and its public OpenAPI document is available. when A client reads the document's paths. then The response path list contains API operations and no product web-app screen routes.\",\n    \"Given The delivered API repository and a running application. when A person reviews the application's exposed routes and browser-visible pages. then No product web-app screen is present; the Swagger page is limited to API documentation and testing.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The public API remains conformant to the locked OpenAPI contract for every declared operation.\",\n  \"Database model deployment preserves every record that exists in the App database before deployment.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-7 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nRestate the change."}